// A struct FIELD whose type is a value-union BOX (`i32 | null`, `f64 | null`, `string | i32`)
// has no equality core, at the plain-struct spelling and inside a union arm alike.
//
//   emitProgram: unsupported struct field type in equality
//
// `vl check` returns 0, so this is a clause-2 violation by construction. silent-class
// inventory D1290.
//
// IT IS THE BOX, NOT THE NULL, and D1180's guard is deliberately not the answer. A
// `(ref null $H)` NICHE field compares as its non-null twin's core under a null guard, and
// every such rep runs today — `string | null`, `Inner | null`, `i32[] | null`,
// `string[] | null`, `f64[] | null`, `i64[] | null`. Code 16 is a `{tag, value}` box: two
// cells with a discriminant, whose compare is a tag compare plus a per-member payload
// compare. A core to build, not a guard to open.
//
// The checker admits the field because `T | null` is value-comparable exactly when `T` is
// (DECISIONS.md); before that ruling this shape was a loud CHECK reject claiming the field
// was not value-comparable, which was false about the design.
//
// Should print true then false.
type A = { d: i32 | null }

const same1: A = { d: 3 }
const same2: A = { d: 3 }
const diff: A = { d: 4 }
print(same1 == same2)
print(same1 == diff)
